1
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:12,267
What's the situation at Point A?

2
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:16,600
Target identified. He's
highly agitated right now.

3
00:00:29,633 --> 00:00:31,067
Don't do anything rash, Takoi.

4
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,200
We need to tread carefully here.

5
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:37,367
I'm ready to breach and
assist at any moment.

6
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:47,233
Hang in there, I'm coming to save you.

7
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,800
He's making a move!

8
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Takoi-san!

9
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,133
- Takoi!
- Takoi-san!

10
00:01:20,633 --> 00:01:22,033
Freeze!

11
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:30,533
Mommy will be here in just a second.

12
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:33,600
Good girl.

13
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:35,233
Mizore...

14
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:38,367
- Okay...
- Here we go...

15
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:43,833
Ma'am, you really need
to keep her collar fastened.

16
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:45,500
You're right.

17
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,967
I'm so sorry, Mizore...

18
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:51,500
Thank you so much for your help, Takoi-san.

19
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,767
All in a day's work catching a dog.

20
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:57,900
But I'm glad she's safe.

21
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,633
Even if it's just a dog, you can't let
your guard down. Lesson learned.

22
00:02:02,367 --> 00:02:03,467
You see?

23
00:02:03,733 --> 00:02:05,933
No matter how small the case is,

24
00:02:06,033 --> 00:02:08,367
you have to take
responsibility and see it through.

25
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:10,200
That's a detective's duty.

26
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:12,200
- Got it?
- Yes, sir!

27
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:14,600
To become a detective like you, Takoi-san,

28
00:02:14,625 --> 00:02:15,958
I'll give it my all.

29
00:02:16,663 --> 00:02:17,910
Like me?

30
00:02:19,067 --> 00:02:20,500
Oh, stop flattering me.

31
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:23,733
Thank you so much, Takoi-san.

32
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:26,933
By the way, next time you
come in, karaoke is on the house.

33
00:02:27,033 --> 00:02:28,443
You have to come visit the shop again.

34
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:29,967
Ma'am...

35
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,267
This is a police station.
Please mind the setting.

36
00:02:32,367 --> 00:02:35,433
It's only because you
haven't visited lately.

37
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,667
All right, all right,
I'll drop by next time.

38
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,800
I'll be waiting for you.

39
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,933
Everyone else is welcome
to come support us too!

40
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:44,600
Will do.

41
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:45,800
Thank you all.

42
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,500
All right...

43
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,367
- Thanks.
- Stay safe.

44
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:49,000
Thank you.

45
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:55,933
Congratulations.

46
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:57,800
Congratulations.

47
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,133
Congrats.

48
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,667
He's the one who stopped
that cyberattack a while back.

49
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:07,433
I heard he also took down
a major nationally wanted crime syndicate.

50
00:03:09,767 --> 00:03:11,233
Community Safety Division.

51
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:14,400
He's the pride of our precinct.

52
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:19,567
Guys from the Cybercrime
Division are a different breed.

53
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:25,267
As expected of the elite
track. Truly impressive.

54
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:29,267
They're on a whole other
level from us frontline grunts.

55
00:03:29,367 --> 00:03:32,500
Should we go butter him up? Just kidding.

56
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,009
- I'll be right back.
- Please wait a moment.

57
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:35,543
- So right now...
- Hurry up and bring him here!

58
00:03:35,567 --> 00:03:37,545
We're still verifying his identity.

59
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:39,533
I can't do this anymore.

60
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:41,967
Do you understand? Bring him out now!

61
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:45,733
I won't be satisfied until I
beat the crap out of him.

62
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,800
Bring him out here!

63
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,000
Alright.

64
00:04:00,933 --> 00:04:03,333
What the hell are you waiting for?

65
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:04,000
Go get him right now!

66
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,667
He's a criminal!

67
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:15,333
Your husband is a
suspect in an assault case.

68
00:04:16,367 --> 00:04:17,667
I don't know.

69
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:19,700
Excuse me.

70
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,433
How could you say something
like that in front of a child?

71
00:04:28,733 --> 00:04:30,067
Hello.

72
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:31,700
Hi there.

73
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,967
That man there is exhausted
from running around.

74
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:37,033
Want to come get some juice with me?

75
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:50,067
If you don't mind, let's go sit over there.

76
00:04:51,167 --> 00:04:52,567
Sound good?

77
00:04:53,467 --> 00:04:56,033
- Yeah.
- All right, let's go.

78
00:04:59,767 --> 00:05:01,733
He's still just a suspect right now.

79
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,600
I'll go grab that juice for you.

80
00:05:13,533 --> 00:05:15,000
Here you go.

81
00:05:16,433 --> 00:05:18,000
Thank you.

82
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,267
This one's for you.

83
00:05:19,367 --> 00:05:20,600
Thanks.

84
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,233
He's just a natural at that.

85
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:26,900
Being too good at winning
people over is a crime in itself.

86
00:05:27,533 --> 00:05:31,700
Ah, that hits the spot.

87
00:05:33,467 --> 00:05:34,867
Gotcha.

88
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:36,967
You guys...

89
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,100
What should we do about this?

90
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:50,067
Bang...

91
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,933
"Duty First Kiss Later"

92
00:06:24,233 --> 00:06:27,933
(Episode 1)

93
00:06:30,767 --> 00:06:34,167
As expected of the most popular
guy at Yama-no-michi Police Station.

94
00:06:34,267 --> 00:06:35,800
Takoi Heisuke.

95
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,567
Egawa, are you making fun of me again?

96
00:06:37,667 --> 00:06:40,367
No way, I'm complimenting
you on how popular you are.

97
00:06:40,467 --> 00:06:42,067
That's not what being popular is about.

98
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:43,067
Huh?

99
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:48,033
A guy like me
should be exactly your type, right?

100
00:06:48,133 --> 00:06:49,733
Like what?

101
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:51,400
Like...

102
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,200
I used to like them older,

103
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,533
Now I prefer them younger,
they look sweet and well-behaved.

104
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:01,400
If we're talking actresses,
like the one who was in "Gokusen"...

105
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:08,260
Here are the investigation files to be
transferred to the Criminal Affairs Division.

106
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:12,300
Yeah, thanks.

107
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:17,300
Must be nice. The Criminal Affairs
Division seems like a lot of fun.

108
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,533
Huh?

109
00:07:19,233 --> 00:07:23,833
Oh, I mean Takoi-san's job.

110
00:07:23,933 --> 00:07:25,133
My bad.

111
00:07:27,467 --> 00:07:28,833
Huh?

112
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:31,800
Did I just get totally roasted?

113
00:07:32,767 --> 00:07:34,000
What?

114
00:07:53,533 --> 00:07:55,567
What's his deal?

115
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,667
Hey.

116
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,833
Keep buttering me up.

117
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:02,467
Don't get so full of yourself.

118
00:08:03,767 --> 00:08:05,300
You're just jealous.

119
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,433
Can't blame him,
Takoi is just that popular.

120
00:08:07,533 --> 00:08:08,700
Oh, please.

121
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:11,067
This isn't even about
being jealous anymore.

122
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:12,500
Oh?

123
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,333
Stop whining here every night.

124
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:16,576
It's about time you settled down.

125
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,267
Exactly.

126
00:08:17,367 --> 00:08:18,600
I want to.

127
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,200
But how should I put it?

128
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,500
Hmm?

129
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,400
A girl I used to date

130
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,940
told me, "She's my friend,
so you need to get along with her."

131
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,033
She introduced me to
one of her female friends.

132
00:08:31,133 --> 00:08:33,733
I did as she asked and got along with her.

133
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:35,367
But we got along a little too well.

134
00:08:35,467 --> 00:08:38,100
Then she said, "You like her, don't you?"

135
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,640
Why does it always end up like this?

136
00:08:42,033 --> 00:08:44,133
Women are such a hassle.

137
00:08:47,467 --> 00:08:49,667
You just haven't met the
right one yet, have you?

138
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:55,467
Someone you'd willingly let
wrap you around her little finger.

139
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:59,500
Well said, boss.

140
00:09:00,367 --> 00:09:01,867
Shut up.

141
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:05,833
Man, being handsome
really does make a difference.

142
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:07,167
It really does.

143
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:08,400
Is that so?

144
00:09:36,633 --> 00:09:38,067
(Mr. Shiono Shu)

145
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:39,633
What the hell are you doing?

146
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:49,500
What are you doing?

147
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,767
Your package was blocking
my door. It's in the way.

148
00:09:54,867 --> 00:09:56,443
Please don't touch my stuff without asking.

149
00:09:56,467 --> 00:10:01,100
What do you mean? You're
the one causing a problem.

150
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:04,000
What's your problem?

151
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:05,333
Yes?

152
00:10:05,433 --> 00:10:06,633
That look in your eyes...

153
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:09,867
This is just how my face looks.

154
00:10:12,867 --> 00:10:14,400
Takoyaki again?

155
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,433
What does it matter? I like it.

156
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:18,100
Oh, is that so?

157
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,633
Look who's talking, Takoi-san.

158
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:22,267
Coming home drunk every single night.

159
00:10:22,367 --> 00:10:23,733
You're almost forty, aren't you?

160
00:10:24,133 --> 00:10:26,373
Careful you don't balloon
into a chubby middle-aged guy.

161
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:29,000
You little...

162
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:46,100
That guy Shiono...

163
00:11:03,967 --> 00:11:06,867
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

164
00:11:07,533 --> 00:11:09,176
(Scams Impersonating
Police Officers Are on the Rise!)

165
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,900
What the hell?

166
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:15,300
Hmm... Did I do something to piss him off?

167
00:11:16,367 --> 00:11:18,233
I really don't get it.

168
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:20,567
I don't know, why?

169
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:24,233
Why is Shiono giving you the cold shoulder?

170
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:27,643
Is it because I'm not on the elite track?

171
00:11:27,667 --> 00:11:28,200
No.

172
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,167
Because I'm too loud?

173
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:31,400
Probably not.

174
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,333
Think about it carefully.

175
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:38,100
Could it be that he just hates me?

176
00:11:47,967 --> 00:11:48,500
Egawa.

177
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:51,367
- Oh.
- I got it. You can't reach, right?

178
00:11:51,467 --> 00:11:53,200
Oh, thanks.

179
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:56,167
Did I say something weird just now?

180
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,333
No, what exactly did I do?

181
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:04,700
Takoi-san.

182
00:12:05,867 --> 00:12:07,200
Takoi-san.

183
00:12:08,233 --> 00:12:09,967
Mr. Yamada.

184
00:12:10,367 --> 00:12:11,033
What brings you here today?

185
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:12,500
I have a favor to ask you.

186
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,700
A favor?

187
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:16,367
Would you go on a blind
date with my granddaughter?

188
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:17,567
Huh?

189
00:12:17,667 --> 00:12:19,633
She just moved back from Tokyo a while ago.

190
00:12:19,733 --> 00:12:21,876
She said she wants to find
someone here and get married.

191
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:23,467
Give me a break, please.

192
00:12:23,567 --> 00:12:24,567
Come on, now.

193
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,667
No, seriously, look.

194
00:12:26,767 --> 00:12:28,567
She's very cute.

195
00:12:28,667 --> 00:12:30,600
She looks exactly like my late wife.

196
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,476
How am I supposed to
respond to that? All right, all right.

197
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:34,867
At least look at her picture.

198
00:12:34,967 --> 00:12:37,200
This is a police station, sir.

199
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:39,167
Let me walk you home. Come on, let's go.

200
00:12:39,267 --> 00:12:41,767
Excuse us.

201
00:12:42,833 --> 00:12:45,600
Just look at her picture,
at least give it a glance.

202
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:46,533
No, thanks.

203
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:47,700
Why not?

204
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,543
What if she turns out
to be exactly my type?

205
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:51,200
Wouldn't that be a good thing?

206
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:54,167
What if I actually end up
becoming in-laws with Mr. Yamada?

207
00:12:54,567 --> 00:12:56,533
You're overthinking this, Takoi.

208
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:03,500
Yagi-san.

209
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,500
Just give her a call.

210
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,833
Thanks.

211
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,833
I'll leave it to you then.

212
00:13:32,233 --> 00:13:32,800
I'll be going now.

213
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:33,900
Alright, good work today.

214
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Good work.

215
00:13:35,067 --> 00:13:36,067
- Wait.
- Yeah?

216
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:37,433
Want to grab a drink today?

217
00:13:37,533 --> 00:13:38,533
Sorry.

218
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:40,800
I have a date with my wife today.

219
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:42,467
Oh, I see.

220
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,367
Yagi-san.

221
00:13:47,467 --> 00:13:51,767
It's my daughter's birthday today.

222
00:13:51,867 --> 00:13:52,967
Good work today.

223
00:13:53,067 --> 00:13:54,767
Good work.

224
00:13:59,667 --> 00:14:02,200
Sorry, I'm heading home
to play video games.

225
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,800
Good work.

226
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:07,567
Good work.

227
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,767
Ah, that hits the spot.

228
00:14:18,033 --> 00:14:21,000
No one making dinner for you today?

229
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:22,200
Don't I have you, boss?

230
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,633
I mean someone who
cooks specifically for you.

231
00:14:25,733 --> 00:14:29,667
Boss, are you trying to drive
away a valued customer?

232
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:33,667
Well, you won't have any
luck just hanging around here.

233
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:36,200
That has nothing to do with it.

234
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:39,033
They say your destined one...

235
00:14:39,133 --> 00:14:42,767
Always appears at the perfect time.

236
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,867
Destined one?

237
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:46,767
I'm already 38.

238
00:14:46,867 --> 00:14:48,767
Age is just a number.

239
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:50,233
No way.

240
00:14:50,333 --> 00:14:53,633
The thought of dating at
my age is just exhausting.

241
00:14:53,733 --> 00:14:58,133
So you plan to spend the
rest of your life all alone here?

242
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,033
Well, that's true...

243
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:04,700
I don't want that.

244
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,167
Yeah.

245
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,833
It hurts. Help me.

246
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:50,233
I'm all alone here.

247
00:15:52,133 --> 00:15:53,867
I have a date with my wife today.

248
00:15:53,967 --> 00:15:56,633
It's my daughter's birthday today.

249
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,267
I'm home.

250
00:16:20,033 --> 00:16:23,033
I have to get married.

251
00:16:35,367 --> 00:16:36,167
Takoi-san.

252
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:38,033
Oh, Mr. Yamada.

253
00:16:38,133 --> 00:16:39,467
What's up?

254
00:16:39,567 --> 00:16:41,500
I brought her here.

255
00:16:44,067 --> 00:16:45,533
Takoi-san.

256
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,333
Nice to meet you.

257
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:52,333
Thank you for always
taking care of my grandpa.

258
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:54,267
This is my granddaughter, Haruka.

259
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:58,833
Nice to meet you, I'm Takoi.

260
00:16:58,933 --> 00:17:03,100
Well? My granddaughter
is pretty, isn't she?

261
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,667
Grandpa, stop it.

262
00:17:04,767 --> 00:17:07,800
Yes, she's absolutely gorgeous.

263
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:12,400
What brings you here today?

264
00:17:13,067 --> 00:17:15,176
You turned me down before
even looking at her picture.

265
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,876
So I figured I'd just bring her in person.

266
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,609
I thought meeting face-to-face
would be the quickest way.

267
00:17:18,633 --> 00:17:20,800
I'm sorry for the trouble.

268
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:22,633
Not at all, it's just...

269
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:24,833
It's been pretty quiet today.

270
00:17:24,933 --> 00:17:27,033
I was just thinking how nice that is.

271
00:17:27,133 --> 00:17:27,967
That's good.

272
00:17:28,067 --> 00:17:30,100
I'll leave the rest to you young folks.

273
00:17:43,933 --> 00:17:44,700
Um...

274
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:45,433
Yes?

275
00:17:45,533 --> 00:17:49,300
If you don't mind, let's
exchange contact info.

276
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,333
Sure, I'd love to.

277
00:17:51,433 --> 00:17:51,900
Great.

278
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,367
Uh, so...

279
00:17:53,467 --> 00:17:54,967
Well...

280
00:17:59,933 --> 00:18:04,067
Oh, sorry to interrupt.

281
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:22,133
I'll be taking off for today.

282
00:18:22,233 --> 00:18:23,900
See you, Takoi-san.

283
00:18:30,033 --> 00:18:31,733
Hey.

284
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:35,567
Someone asked me to change the bulletin.

285
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:39,067
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

286
00:18:39,933 --> 00:18:41,500
Are you going to date her?

287
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:42,833
Huh?

288
00:18:43,133 --> 00:18:44,967
How should I know?

289
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,500
What's it to you?

290
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:49,500
Is she your type?

291
00:18:50,933 --> 00:18:52,967
Ah...

292
00:18:53,067 --> 00:18:54,300
She is my type.

293
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,067
Spot on.

294
00:18:56,167 --> 00:18:57,176
And she seems really nice, too.

295
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,767
Oh, really?

296
00:18:58,867 --> 00:18:59,667
What?

297
00:18:59,767 --> 00:19:01,533
What, you got a problem with that?

298
00:19:02,267 --> 00:19:05,233
Why don't you just date everyone then?

299
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:06,700
Huh?

300
00:19:07,233 --> 00:19:10,833
You treat everyone exactly the same.

301
00:19:10,933 --> 00:19:12,733
And you're way too nosy.

302
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:15,233
What are you talking about?

303
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,500
For a cop...

304
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:21,100
You meddle too much in
other people's business.

305
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,900
No, I'm just...

306
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,376
Interacting with everyone normally.

307
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,700
Huh?

308
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:27,867
Normally?

309
00:19:27,967 --> 00:19:29,400
You mean agreeing to a blind date?

310
00:19:31,367 --> 00:19:34,000
That was... Mr. Yamada forcing it on me.

311
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:35,700
Elementary schoolers.

312
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:37,600
The elderly.

313
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:39,700
A suspect's wife.

314
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,109
You get way too close to everyone.

315
00:19:41,133 --> 00:19:42,533
You care too much about others.

316
00:19:42,633 --> 00:19:44,433
Do you even have any
self-awareness as a cop?

317
00:19:44,467 --> 00:19:45,867
Do you?

318
00:19:45,967 --> 00:19:47,767
Seriously, you...

319
00:19:47,867 --> 00:19:50,067
You only do this stuff because
you lack self-awareness.

320
00:19:51,633 --> 00:19:53,600
Everyone calls you a good guy.

321
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,967
Don't tell me you
actually enjoy that feeling?

322
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:57,933
Hold it right there.

323
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,633
Come here.

324
00:20:16,767 --> 00:20:18,133
Sit down.

325
00:20:27,433 --> 00:20:28,900
So?

326
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,933
What?

327
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,933
Why are you always picking on me?

328
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,633
Did I do something to you?

329
00:20:40,333 --> 00:20:41,967
Let me ask you this instead.

330
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,833
Why do you think?

331
00:20:47,233 --> 00:20:51,200
”Why do you think?”

332
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:54,133
I'm the one asking you.

333
00:21:03,233 --> 00:21:05,967
I know you don't like me.

334
00:21:06,067 --> 00:21:08,367
But honestly, it's hard
to work together like this.

335
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,667
Let's just lay it all out on the table.

336
00:21:16,633 --> 00:21:18,633
Be honest.

337
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,400
Just say whatever is on your mind.

338
00:21:31,167 --> 00:21:32,933
What, you want to fight?

339
00:21:44,167 --> 00:21:46,033
Wait, don't...

340
00:21:49,167 --> 00:21:52,433
Even if you play rough, I won't back down.

341
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:17,533
(This story is purely fictional.)

342
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:20,740
(Next Episode)
He's mine, so don't get the wrong idea.

343
00:22:20,833 --> 00:22:22,267
What is your deal?

344
00:22:22,967 --> 00:22:24,033
Why do you think?

345
00:22:24,133 --> 00:22:25,833
There's only one reason.

346
00:22:25,933 --> 00:22:27,267
Because I like you.

347
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:28,833
Huh?

348
00:22:28,867 --> 00:22:30,833
I like you, Takoi-san.

349
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:32,633
Me?

350
00:22:35,533 --> 00:22:36,932
I've always had my eyes on you.

351
00:22:36,933 --> 00:22:38,033
Takoi-san.

